.TH ARCH-TRACKER 1 "2026-11-23" "arch-tracker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arch-tracker \- local screen-time and activity tracker for KDE Plasma on Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arch-tracker
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arch-tracker
records which apps, sites, terminal programs and AI agents you use, and for how long,
without sending anything off the computer.
A per-user daemon, started by the systemd user unit
.BR arch-tracker.service ,
watches KWin, idle time, the screen lock, media and the browser extension, and writes
raw intervals to a local SQLite database.
What counts as screen time is decided when you look at the data, so changing a setting
re-classifies all history.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the tracker in the foreground (normally started by systemd).
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Show what is being tracked right now and which sources work.
.TP
.BR pause " [" \fIduration\fR ]
Pause tracking, for example
.B pause 30m
or
.BR "pause 1h" .
Without a duration, tracking stays paused until
.BR resume .
.TP
.B resume
Resume tracking.
.TP
.BR open " [" \fIpage\fR ]
Open the dashboard in the default browser, signed in.
.I page
is one of today, apps, agents, trends or settings.
.TP
.B setup
Unpack the browser extensions and register the native-messaging bridge for every
installed Chromium- and Firefox-based browser.
.TP
.B doctor
Check every data source and explain how to fix problems.
.TP
.BR serve " [" \-\-db " \fIfile\fR] [" \-\-port " \fIport\fR]"
Read-only dashboard for a database (for example a copy from another computer).
.TP
.BR export " \-\-from " \fIdate\fR " [" \-\-to " \fIdate\fR] [" \-\-format " csv|json]"
Print every recorded interval in a date range (dates as YYYY-MM-DD).
.SH DASHBOARD
The dashboard is served at
.BI http://arch-tracker.localhost: port /
(port 7600 by default) and only answers on the loopback interface.
It is locked: open it from the tray icon or with
.BR "arch-tracker open" ,
which signs the browser in with a one-time code.
The browser then stays signed in, so bookmarks keep working.
Other programs on the computer cannot read your history.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/arch-tracker/config.toml
Settings. Edited here or in the dashboard; changes apply immediately.
.TP
.I ~/.config/arch-tracker/custom.css
Extra CSS loaded by the dashboard.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/arch-tracker/tracker.db
The recorded intervals.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/arch-tracker/dashboard.key
The dashboard's sign-in key (mode 0600). Delete it and restart the daemon to sign
every browser out.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/arch-tracker/
Control and browser-bridge sockets.
.SH PRIVACY
Browser data is the host name and page title only, never paths or queries.
Private (incognito) windows count as time with no site, title or audio details.
Terminal data is the program name and project folder only, never arguments or
environment variables.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
.PP
https://github.com/abhimangs/arch-tracker
